{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRoBGRGPAfXfgpEPJXdV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8FSJWKQDqPM3RbZLpZAec","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > diagnosis.json <<'EOF'\n{\"spec_element\": \"invariant\",\n \"proof_obligation\": \"preservation\",\n \"diagnosis\": \"The bounds invariant 0<=n<=a.Length+1 is too weak: it allows n == a.Length+1, so in the second invariant 'forall i :: 0<=i<n ==> e!=a[i]' the index i can reach a.Length and a[i] is out of range (well-formedness failure at line 10). The loop guard n != a.Length and the increment n := n+1 mean n never exceeds a.Length, so the correct invariant is 0<=n<=a.Length. With it, the quantifier is well-formed, the invariant is maintained, and on exit (n == a.Length) the second invariant contradicts the precondition, so the post-loop path is unreachable.\"}\nEOF\nsed -i 's/invariant 0<=n<= (a.Length) + 1/invariant 0<=n<=a.Length/' program.dfy && dafny verify program.dfy"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":22420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":364,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83f0ced8-c873-4298-896b-25f0e3a137ce","uuid":"f50e8e55-d19b-4459-9701-c953d27d38e6","timestamp":"2026-10-27T00:29:50.175Z","request_id":"req_011CgRoBG7ASSUTKw5SKQ7Nt"}
